outputs.L1:
Disclosed is a method for processing cocoa beans or nibs, comprising the following steps:

(a) adding water to the cocoa beans or nibs to form a suspension;

(b) wet-grinding the suspension;

(c) subjecting the suspension to heat treatment at a temperature of 70°C or less;

(d) separating the suspension into a water phase (heavy phase), a fat phase (light phase) comprising cocoa butter, and a solid phase comprising cocoa powder and fluid components; and

(e) continuously separating the fluid components from the solid phase obtained in step (d) to obtain cocoa aroma and cocoa powder by supplying a continuous flow of the solid phase to a mixing device;

wherein the mixing device comprises:

- a cylindrical tubular body having a horizontal axis, an inlet opening for the solid phase, an outlet opening for the dried solid phase, and an optional outlet opening for a vapor phase comprising cocoa aroma;
- end plates closing the tubular body at its opposite ends;
- a coaxial jacket configured to heat or cool the internal wall of the tubular body to a temperature ranging from 55°C to 150°C; and
- a bladed rotor rotatably supported within the tubular body, the blades of the rotor being helically arranged and oriented to centrifuge the solid phase while simultaneously transporting it toward the outlet opening.

outputs.L2:
A cocoa bean or nib processing method includes the following operations:

(a) combining the cocoa beans or nibs with water to produce a suspension;  
(b) grinding the suspension while wet;  
(c) heating the suspension at a temperature no higher than 70°C;  
(d) dividing the suspension into three fractions: a heavy aqueous phase, a light fat phase containing cocoa butter, and a solids phase containing cocoa powder and liquid constituents; and  
(e) continuously removing the liquid constituents from the solids phase produced in step (d), thereby yielding cocoa powder and cocoa aroma, by feeding a continuous stream of the solids phase into a mixing apparatus.

The mixing apparatus includes:

- a horizontally oriented cylindrical tube provided with a solids-phase inlet, a dried-solids outlet, and, optionally, a vapor outlet for a vapor phase containing cocoa aroma;
- end plates sealing the tube at both ends;
- a coaxial heating or cooling jacket configured to maintain the tube’s inner wall at between 55°C and 150°C; and
- a rotatable bladed rotor mounted within the tube, with helically arranged blades positioned to centrifuge the solids phase while conveying it toward the outlet.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A method for processing cocoa beans, the method comprising:**  

   providing dehulled cocoa bean material comprising cocoa nibs;  

   wet grinding the cocoa bean material in the presence of water to form a pumpable cocoa slurry;  

   continuously passing the cocoa slurry through a mixing device comprising a processing chamber and a driven bladed rotor disposed in the processing chamber, the bladed rotor subjecting the cocoa slurry to mixing and shear while maintaining the cocoa slurry at a temperature not greater than 70°C;  

   removing an aroma-containing volatile fraction from the cocoa slurry during or after passage through the mixing device and condensing the aroma-containing volatile fraction to obtain a cocoa aroma fraction;  

   separating the treated cocoa slurry into at least a fat-containing phase, an aqueous phase, and a cocoa-solids-containing phase;  

   recovering cocoa butter from the fat-containing phase;  

   recovering water from the aqueous phase; and  

   drying and comminuting the cocoa-solids-containing phase to produce cocoa powder,  

   thereby separately obtaining cocoa butter, cocoa powder, water, and the cocoa aroma fraction while maintaining the cocoa bean material below 70°C.

1. **A cocoa-processing system**, comprising:  

   a jacketed tubular body extending along a longitudinal axis between an upstream feed end and a downstream discharge end, the tubular body defining an internal processing chamber and including a heat-transfer jacket configured to circulate a thermal fluid and maintain an inner wall of the tubular body at a processing temperature of **55°C to 150°C**;  

   a cocoa-material inlet arranged to introduce cocoa solids containing moisture and volatile cocoa-aroma compounds into the processing chamber adjacent the upstream feed end;  

   a rotatable shaft extending longitudinally within the processing chamber;  

   a helical blade assembly carried by the rotatable shaft and comprising at least one helically extending blade having an outer blade edge spaced from or in wiping proximity to the inner wall, the shaft and the helical blade assembly being rotatable at a speed sufficient to:  
   - impart centrifugal acceleration to the cocoa solids and form a dynamically agitated layer of the cocoa solids against the heated inner wall;  
   - advance the cocoa solids from the upstream feed end toward the downstream discharge end;  
   - repeatedly lift, redistribute, and expose the cocoa solids to heat within the processing chamber; and  
   - promote evaporation of moisture and liberation of the volatile cocoa-aroma compounds from the cocoa solids;  

   a drive operatively coupled to the rotatable shaft and configured to control rotational speed of the helical blade assembly independently of the processing temperature, thereby controlling centrifugal force, residence time, solids conveying rate, and drying intensity;  

   a dried-solids outlet positioned adjacent the downstream discharge end and configured to discharge cocoa solids having a moisture content lower than that of the cocoa solids introduced through the cocoa-material inlet;  

   a vapor outlet in fluid communication with the processing chamber and configured to withdraw a vapor stream comprising water vapor and the liberated volatile cocoa-aroma compounds;  

   a gas-separation circuit coupled to the vapor outlet and comprising at least one condenser maintained at a temperature below a dew point of at least a portion of the volatile cocoa-aroma compounds, the gas-separation circuit being configured to separate the vapor stream into an aroma-containing condensate and a residual gas stream;  

   an aroma-recovery vessel fluidly coupled to the gas-separation circuit and configured to collect the aroma-containing condensate for subsequent addition to a cocoa product or use as a cocoa-aroma composition; and  

   a controller operatively coupled to the heat-transfer jacket and the drive, the controller being configured to maintain the inner wall at a selected temperature within the range of 55°C to 150°C and to regulate rotation of the helical blade assembly such that the cocoa solids are simultaneously centrifuged against the inner wall, conveyed longitudinally through the tubular body, and dried while at least a portion of the volatile cocoa-aroma compounds released during drying is recovered through the vapor outlet and the gas-separation circuit.
